{"name":"Water Hyacinth","hex":"#a0a3d2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"water hyacinth","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the genus Pontederia (syn. Eichhornia) of aquatic flowering plants.","especially common water hyacinth (Pontederia crassipes, syn. Eichhornia crassipes), a problematic invasive plant that clogs waterways in warm temperate and subtropical regions worldwide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/water_hyacinth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pontederia crassipes","blocks":[{"text":"Pontederia crassipes, commonly known as common water hyacinth, is an aquatic plant native to South America, naturalized throughout the world, and often invasive outside its native range. It is the sole species of the subgenus Oshunae within the genus Pontederia. Anecdotally, it is known as the \"terror of Bengal\" due to its invasive growth tendencies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Eichhornia_crassipes_C.jpg/330px-Eichhornia_crassipes_C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pontederia_crassipes"},{"title":"Water","blocks":[{"text":"Water is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula H2O. It is a transparent, tasteless, odorless, and nearly colorless chemical substance. It is the main constituent of Earth's streams, lakes, and oceans. Water is also the fluid of all known living organisms, in which it acts as a solvent. Water, being a polar molecule, undergoes strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding which is a large contributor to its physical and chemical properties. It is vital for all known forms of life, despite not providing food energy or being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/H2O_2D_labelled.svg/330px-H2O_2D_labelled.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water"},{"title":"Hyacinth","blocks":[{"text":"Hyacinthus is a genus of bulbous herbs and spring-blooming perennials. They are fragrant flowering plants in the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Scilloideae and are commonly called hyacinths. The genus is native predominantly to the Eastern Mediterranean region from the south of Turkey to the Palestine region, although naturalized more widely."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Hyacinth_-_Anglesey_Abbey.jpg/330px-Hyacinth_-_Anglesey_Abbey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyacinth"},{"title":"Color of water","blocks":[{"text":"The color of water varies with the ambient conditions in which that water is present. While relatively small quantities of water appear to be colorless and transparent, pure water has a slight blue color that becomes deeper as the thickness of the observed sample increases. The hue of water is an intrinsic property and is caused by selective absorption and scattering of blue light. Dissolved elements or suspended impurities may give water a different color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG/330px-Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_of_water"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Kenya_Kisumu_Harbour_Hyacinths_1997ke09b21.jpg/500px-Kenya_Kisumu_Harbour_Hyacinths_1997ke09b21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Kenya_Kisumu_Harbour_Hyacinths_1997ke09b21.jpg/500px-Kenya_Kisumu_Harbour_Hyacinths_1997ke09b21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Water hyacinth at Kisumu Port","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKenya_Kisumu_Harbour_Hyacinths_1997ke09b21.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Water_Hyacinth_choking_the_Haldia_Municipality_Pool_at_South_Bengal.jpg/500px-Water_Hyacinth_choking_the_Haldia_Municipality_Pool_at_South_Bengal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Water_Hyacinth_choking_the_Haldia_Municipality_Pool_at_South_Bengal.jpg/1280px-Water_Hyacinth_choking_the_Haldia_Municipality_Pool_at_South_Bengal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Water_Hyacinth_choking_the_Haldia_Municipality_Pool_at_South_Bengal.jpg/500px-Water_Hyacinth_choking_the_Haldia_Municipality_Pool_at_South_Bengal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haldia Municipality Pool, a public water reservoir is being choked by growing water hyacinth population as in December 2019.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_Hyacinth_choking_the_Haldia_Municipality_Pool_at_South_Bengal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/The_Eruption_of_Taal_Volcano_on_it%27s_3rd_day.jpg/500px-The_Eruption_of_Taal_Volcano_on_it%27s_3rd_day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/The_Eruption_of_Taal_Volcano_on_it%27s_3rd_day.jpg/1280px-The_Eruption_of_Taal_Volcano_on_it%27s_3rd_day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/The_Eruption_of_Taal_Volcano_on_it%27s_3rd_day.jpg/500px-The_Eruption_of_Taal_Volcano_on_it%27s_3rd_day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ash-covered blooming water hyacinth along the lakeshore in San Nicolas, Batangas, Philippines due to the eruption of Taal Volcano in the distance.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Eruption_of_Taal_Volcano_on_it's_3rd_day.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/LucbinhTienGiang.jpg/500px-LucbinhTienGiang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/LucbinhTienGiang.jpg/1280px-LucbinhTienGiang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/LucbinhTienGiang.jpg/500px-LucbinhTienGiang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Water hyacinth on a canal in Tien Giang province, Vietnam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALucbinhTienGiang.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Berky_M%C3%A4hsammelboot_Typ_6520.jpg/500px-Berky_M%C3%A4hsammelboot_Typ_6520.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Berky_M%C3%A4hsammelboot_Typ_6520.jpg/1280px-Berky_M%C3%A4hsammelboot_Typ_6520.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Berky_M%C3%A4hsammelboot_Typ_6520.jpg/500px-Berky_M%C3%A4hsammelboot_Typ_6520.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An aquatic weed harvester collects the water plant via conveyor belt on a hold and can unload the material at the shore.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerky_M%C3%A4hsammelboot_Typ_6520.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Megamelus_scutellaris_biocontrol.jpg/250px-Megamelus_scutellaris_biocontrol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/14/Megamelus_scutellaris_biocontrol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Megamelus_scutellaris_biocontrol.jpg/250px-Megamelus_scutellaris_biocontrol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" In 2010, the insect Megamelus scutellaris was released by the Agricultural Research Service as a biological control for water hyacinth.[113]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMegamelus_scutellaris_biocontrol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Water_hyacinth.jpg/330px-Water_hyacinth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Water_hyacinth.jpg/960px-Water_hyacinth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Water_hyacinth.jpg/330px-Water_hyacinth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_hyacinth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Eichhornia_crassipes.jpg/250px-Eichhornia_crassipes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Eichhornia_crassipes.jpg/330px-Eichhornia_crassipes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Eichhornia_crassipes.jpg/250px-Eichhornia_crassipes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIMG_2365.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}